      "id": "DSD-01",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-discrete-series-derivatives",
      "title": "The derivative filtration and the compact weights it can reach",
      "equations": [
        "global-discrete-series-one-place"
      ],
      "dependencies": [],
      "hypotheses": "Under the indefinite count with n₀≥8, at each archimedean place the unitary discrete-series data have bounded Harish-Chandra parameter |λᵢ|≤b², a specified lowest compact type, and an opposite-sign gap ≥120 n q^(3/2).",
      "statement": "On finite-dimensional spaces of vectors of derivative order ≤P, local compact highest weights differ from λ+ρ_n−ρ_c by Euclidean norm at most √2 P. Differentiation raises order at most once; the one-place norm bound follows by the Casimir calculation below.",
