      "hypotheses": "Use the full and compact Casimir eigenvalues in the smooth unitary module, compact-type decomposition and the finite tensor product over the f real places. N=n² f and the cusp descent starts at P₀=8qN.",
      "statement": "On a single place the derivative is bounded by its Hilbert–Schmidt norm times (√n b² + (3/2)n^(3/2) + 3P) times the vector norm. Across all places there is the additional factor √f for the norm obtained by adding the squares of directions. Monotonicity in P gives the common constant at P₀+N for the Sobolev bound and the descent.",
